.SH NAME
slemu \- headless Second Life / OpenSim region emulator for LSL bytecode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slemu
.RI [ options ]
.IR script.lslbc " [" more.lslbc " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slemu
is the Sakura Studios region emulator. It loads one or more SLBC
bytecode files produced by
.BR lslc (1)
and executes them in a self-contained, headless region with realistic
side-effect mocking: chat is routed between linked scripts, money
transfers debit and credit avatar balances, listens are dispatched by
channel, HTTP can be either stubbed from a fixture file or sent for
real, and persistent state (KVP, linkset data, notecards, inventory)
is held in a directory-shaped
.I volume
that survives across runs.
.PP
Each positional argument is a separate script and becomes a linked
prim in the same simulated object \(em the first script is link 1
(the root prim), subsequent scripts are link 2, 3, ... and may
exchange
.BR llMessageLinked ()
traffic.
.PP
.B slemu
is the engine that powers
.BR lsltest (1)
(scripted property tests) and
.BR lsldb (1)
(interactive line-level debugger; see the
.B \-\-debug
flag below). Used on its own it is also a convenient one-shot
checker: write a script,
.B lslc \-c
it, and run it under
.B slemu
to confirm it boots, enters
.BR default ,
handles a synthetic touch, and exits cleanly.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Region and avatars
.TP
.BI \-\-volume " DIR"
Use
.I DIR
as the persistence root for KVP, linkset data, notecards and HTTP
caches. The directory is created if it does not exist. Defaults to
.IR ./slemu_volume .
.TP
.BI \-\-owner " UUID" [: Name ]
Set the owner avatar's UUID (and optionally display name). This is the
value returned by
.BR llGetOwner ()
and influences ownership-gated built-ins.
.TP
.BI \-\-owner\-balance " N"
Starting L$ balance for the owner avatar. Defaults to
.BR 0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-avatar " UUID" : BAL [: Name ]
Pre-register an additional avatar in the region with a starting L$
balance. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Object name returned by
.BR llGetObjectName ().
Defaults to
.BR Object .
.SS Execution limits
.TP
.BI \-\-steps " N"
Stop after dispatching
.I N
events. The default is
.BR 100000 .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Wall-clock limit in seconds (floating point). The default is
.BR 60 .
.TP
.B \-\-trace
Log every event dispatched to a script's event queue.
.SS HTTP
.TP
.B \-\-no\-http
(Default.) HTTP requests are answered from the in-region fixture
table or, if none matches, with an empty 200 response.
.TP
.B \-\-http\-real
Make real HTTP requests via the system
.BR curl (1)
binary. Use with care: this lets sandboxed bytecode talk to the
network.
.TP
.BI \-\-http\-fixture " FILE"
Load an HTTP fixture file. Each fixture entry is matched against an
outgoing request URL by substring; the first match wins.
.SS World / player simulation
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Load a world-config file. Config files may declare additional
avatars, groups, owner attributes and HTTP fixtures; they are the
right place to describe a multi-avatar scenario.
.TP
.BI \-\-commands " FILE"
Load a command file describing scripted player actions (touch, chat,
pay, give-inventory, sit, ...). Combined with
.B \-\-config
this turns
.B slemu
into a deterministic, repeatable player.
.TP
.B \-\-json\-events
Emit world events on standard output as one JSON object per line.
This is the machine-readable mode used by tooling.
.SS Debugging
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enter the line-level debug protocol on standard input/output. The
protocol is JSON-line in both directions and is intended to be driven
by a front-end such as
.BR lsldb (1).
Implies
.BR \-\-json\-events .
.SS Other
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the
.B slemu
version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Stop option parsing; all following arguments are treated as bytecode
files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a single compiled script with stub HTTP and a fresh volume. The
script's
.BR state_entry ()
fires immediately and any
.B llOwnerSay
or
.B llSay
output is written to standard output:
.PP
.RS
.B slemu greeter.lslbc
.RE
.PP
Enable real HTTP through
.BR curl (1).
Useful when you want to point a script at a local development server
without re-deploying it inside the viewer:
.PP
.RS
.B slemu \-\-http\-real vendor.lslbc
.RE
.PP
Pin HTTP responses to a fixture file for deterministic tests. The
fixture file is plain text; each entry binds a URL substring to a
status code and body, and the first match wins:
.PP
.RS
.B slemu \-\-http\-fixture tests/fixtures/marketplace.txt vendor.lslbc
.RE
.PP
Drive a script as a scripted player. The command file may issue
chats, touches, payments and dialog responses on behalf of named
avatars; combined with
.B \-\-config
this gives a multi-avatar world that runs exactly the same way every
time:
.PP
.RS
.B slemu \-\-config worlds/club.cfg \-\-commands scenarios/buy_one.cmd club_vendor.lslbc
.RE
.PP
Attach an interactive debugger. The
.B \-\-debug
flag turns standard input/output into a JSON-line debug channel;
.BR lsldb (1)
spawns
.B slemu
this way automatically. Direct use is mostly of interest to authors
of alternative front-ends:
.PP
.RS
.B slemu \-\-debug greeter.lslbc
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The region ran to completion and every loaded script exited normally
within the
.B \-\-steps
and
.B \-\-timeout
budgets.
.TP
.B 1
At least one script raised an uncaught runtime error, or a budget was
exceeded.
.TP
.B 2
Driver error: missing or unreadable bytecode, bad fixture/config
file, unwriteable volume, malformed command line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./slemu_volume/
Default persistence directory. Holds per-script KVP, linkset data,
inventory contents, notecards and the HTTP cache. Override with
.BR \-\-volume .
.TP
.IR script .lslbc
SLBC bytecode produced by
.BR "lslc \-c" .
.TP
.I fixtures
Plain-text HTTP fixture files loaded via
.BR \-\-http\-fixture .
.TP
.I config files
World configuration files loaded via
.BR \-\-config .
.TP
.I command files
Scripted player actions loaded via
.BR \-\-commands .
.SH BUGS
.B slemu
is a faithful but not bit-exact emulator: floating-point rounding,
list memory accounting and event scheduling order can differ from
the real Second Life simulator under heavy load. For most
correctness testing the difference is invisible; for performance
tuning it is not a substitute for measuring inside the viewer.
.PP
The
.B \-\-http\-real
mode shells out to
.BR curl (1)
and inherits its TLS/proxy configuration; there is no per-request
sandbox.
.PP
Please report bugs to
